{"id":29208,"slug":"revenge","title":"Revenge","year":1989,"country":"Kazakhstan","duration":99,"spine":876,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29208-revenge","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/db96c5947256e58c76b29162412c782b/fFzRqS2k4qQ7uYfoJgI45cQIQIScQ3_large.jpg","description":"A child is raised in Korea to avenge the death of his father’s first child in this decades-spanning tale of obsession and violence, the third collaboration between director Ermek Shinarbaev and writer Anatoli Kim. A study of everyday evil infused with philosophy and poetry, this haunting allegory was the first Soviet film to look at the Korean diaspora in central Asia, and a founding work of the Kazakh New Wave. Rigorous and complex, Revenge weaves luminous imagery with inventive narrative elements in an unforgettable meditation on the way trauma is passed down through generations.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Ermek Shinarbaev","slug":"ermek-shinarbaev"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Aleksandr Pan","role":"Sungu, the poet","slug":"aleksandr-pan"},{"actor":"Valentina Tyo","role":"Wife of Yan","slug":"valentina-tyo"},{"actor":"Kasym Zhakibayev","role":"Old Tsai","slug":"kasym-zhakibayev"},{"actor":"Lyubov Germanova","role":"Elza, the Romanian","slug":"lyubov-germanova"},{"actor":"Oleg Li","role":"Old king and old monk","slug":"oleg-li"},{"actor":"Yerik Zholzhaksynov","role":"Young king","slug":"yerik-zholzhaksynov"},{"actor":"Juozas Budraitis","role":"Tall dumb guy","slug":"juozas-budraitis"},{"actor":"Peter Jan","role":"Young Sungu","slug":"peter-jan"},{"actor":"Zinaida Em","role":"Mother of Sungu","slug":"zinaida-em"},{"actor":"Maksim Munzuk","role":"Old Yan","slug":"maksim-munzuk"},{"actor":"Nikolai Tacheyev","role":"Young Yan, teacher","slug":"nikolai-tacheyev"},{"actor":"Li Kham Dek","role":"Old woman in final scene","slug":"li-kham-dek"},{"actor":"Tsoi Ke Suk","role":"Old woman in final scene","slug":"tsoi-ke-suk"},{"actor":"Olga Yenzak","role":"Old